 "processing": [
  "Decoded to mono (channels averaged) at 48 kHz.",
  "accordion only: mixed with itself resampled +12 cents (a second reed, musette), and started where the note reaches a third of its level, with a 6 ms fade-in (the harmonica's breath-in swell cut).",
  "Leading silence trimmed to 1 ms before the onset (2%% of the peak), with a 1 ms fade-in; spoons are cut from one take at the given slice (seconds) first.",
  "Melodic: pitch measured by YIN over the steady part (median of frames), labelled with the nearest semitone, and resampled (ffmpeg aresample soxr) onto it; capped at 2.5 s with a 0.25 s fade-out; peak normalised to -3 dBFS per file.",
  "Percussion: capped at 0.6 s with an 80 ms fade-out; one gain per instrument putting its loudest take's peak at -3 dBFS (the strokes keep their relative levels).",
  "Encoded as Ogg Opus, 64 kbit/s, mono 48 kHz, bit-exact (as tools/audio/install.py)."
 ],
